{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/collections/hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton-local-government-reorganisation","content_id":"db187960-6d5b-407c-adca-5ac949729371","description":"Documents relating to the government’s programme of local government reorganisation in Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><h2 id=\"timeline\">Timeline</h2>\n\n<h4 id=\"february-2025\">5 February 2025</h4>\n\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/local-government-reorganisation-invitation-to-local-authorities-in-two-tier-areas/letter-hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton\">invitation letter</a> sent to Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton councils set out their milestones for reorganisation.</p>\n\n<p>They were invited to submit final proposals by 26 September 2025.</p>\n\n<h4 id=\"november-2025\">19 November 2025</h4>\n\n<p>A <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-statements/detail/2025-11-19/hcws1071\">written ministerial statement</a> was made to Parliament. This set out that a <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/consultations/local-government-reorganisation-in-hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton\">statutory consultation on proposals for local government reorganisation in Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton</a> was published. No changes have been proposed for the Isle of Wight, an existing unitary council.</p>\n\n<p>The Minister of State for Local Government and Homelessness also wrote to the leaders of councils in Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton to thank them for their proposals and inform them of the consultation.</p>\n\n<div role=\"note\" aria-label=\"Information\" class=\"application-notice info-notice\">\n  <p>Gosport Borough Council and Isle of Wight council did not submit proposals for unitary local government and so the letter is not addressed to their leaders.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 id=\"march-2025\">25 March 2025</h4>\n\n<p>A <a rel=\"external\" href=\"https://questions-statements.parliament.uk/written-statements/detail/2026-03-25/hcws1455\">written ministerial statement</a> was made to Parliament, setting out the Secretary of State’s decision to implement the proposal for 5 unitary councils to be established in Hampshire (option 1A).</p>\n\n<p>Secondary legislation, which will be subject to Parliamentary approval, will now be taken forward to abolish existing councils, establish new councils and make transitional arrangements. </p>\n\n<p>​Accompanying this announcement, a letter was sent to <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/local-government-reorganisation-decision-letter-to-hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton-council-leaders\">Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton council leaders</a>.</p>\n\n<h4 id=\"september-2026\">7 September 2026</h4>\n\n<p>On 7 September 2026, the Minister for Local Government, Devolution and Regional Growth wrote to local government reorganisation council leaders.</p>\n\n<p>This letter announced the withdrawal of the current decisions for:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Essex, Southend-on-Sea and Thurrock</li>\n  <li>Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton</li>\n  <li>Norfolk</li>\n  <li>Suffolk</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>It also announced a rapid review of the local government reorganisation programme. This includes decisions taken in July 2026 and the 2 outstanding areas awaiting decisions.</p>\n\n<p>The Secretary of State also announced these measures in an oral statement to Parliament on 7 September 2026.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Review update letter to council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:01:29Z"},{"note":"Programme review and decisions withdrawal letter to council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-09-07T16:03:45Z"},{"note":"Implementation letter to Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton council chief executives added.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-31T09:48:55Z"},{"note":"Decision letter to Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton council leaders added.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-25T13:13:40Z"},{"note":"Letter to council leaders on publicity code added.","public_timestamp":"2025-11-19T16:29:21Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2025-11-19T00:00:00Z"}],"collection_groups":[{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["2e26431f-87f4-4aa3-8a85-0212210137a8"],"title":"Consultations"},{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\">\n</div>","documents":["2d4c8dae-f904-4f01-b20b-5b49dfc9b238","c504c71b-3378-462f-8f9d-a9fc8b5fe09b","2647ecc2-a926-48b6-ae55-2c7fbdabdfbb","10aa27a3-0421-4d3f-8d3a-b50fcf5523f2","ce978c9a-e4a1-4cad-a0fd-dd46e7c638cf","4c76d086-d39a-4d4c-a4d2-04e4a30bbfa0"],"title":"Letters to Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton councils"}],"emphasised_organisations":["1390d07f-12b3-4f55-9dd5-fec5fd9e3649"],"first_public_at":"2025-11-19T00:00:00.000+00:00","headers":[{"id":"timeline","level":2,"text":"Timeline"}],"political":false},"document_type":"document_collection","first_published_at":"2025-11-19T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/collections/hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton-local-government-reorganisation","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/collections/hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton-local-government-reorganisation","base_path":"/government/collections/hampshire-isle-of-wight-portsmouth-and-southampton-local-government-reorganisation","content_id":"db187960-6d5b-407c-adca-5ac949729371","document_type":"document_collection","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-10-29T17:01:29Z","schema_name":"document_collection","title":"Hampshire, Isle of Wight, Portsmouth and Southampton: Local government reorganisation","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/hampshi